From: Docker Hardened Images <dhi@docker.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix spire-agent non-root permissions on /run/spire
Source: https://github.com/cilium/cilium/blob/v1.20.2/install/kubernetes/cilium/templates/spire/agent/daemonset.yaml

kubelet creates every hostPath volume with `DirectoryOrCreate` as root:root,
mode 0755, on the host, and never honors a pod's fsGroup or
runAsUser/runAsGroup for hostPath (fsGroup-based ownership only applies to
volume types kubelet itself manages the lifecycle of, e.g. emptyDir and
CSI/PV-backed volumes - hostPath is a direct passthrough to the host
filesystem and is deliberately left untouched). DHI's values.yaml runs
spire-agent as a non-root podSecurityContext (runAsUser/runAsGroup 65532).

Two directories need to be owned by that uid/gid before the agent container
starts:

- dir(adminSocketPath) (/run/spire/sockets), the hostPath spire-agent mounts
  to create its own "agent" subdirectory and bind agentSocketPath
  (/run/spire/sockets/agent/agent.sock) - without this, the agent fails with
  "create UDS listener: ... bind: permission denied". This chown is
  recursive: /run/spire/sockets is a hostPath, so it persists across pod
  restarts on the same node, and can already contain a stale root-owned
  "agent" subdirectory or socket file left behind by an earlier attempt
  before this fix existed. A non-recursive chown of the parent alone doesn't
  reach pre-existing content.
- /run/spire itself, where spire-agent writes its own state-cache file
  (agent-data.json) directly - without this, the agent fails with "failed to
  write data file: ... permission denied".

/run/spire is not itself a volume upstream - it's just the common parent of
the config/bundle/sockets mounts, auto-created per-container by kubelet.
Since each container in a pod has its own independent root filesystem,
chowning a plain (non-volume-backed) directory in one container is invisible
to every other container - only genuine shared volumes propagate ownership
changes across containers. This patch adds a dedicated `spire-agent-data`
emptyDir volume mounted at /run/spire in both the new initContainer and the
spire-agent container (nesting under the existing, more specific
config/bundle/sockets mounts exactly as Linux mount nesting allows), so the
initContainer's chown of /run/spire is actually visible to spire-agent.
Scoped to a pod-local emptyDir (chowned non-recursively - it's always
freshly empty, no possibility of stale content) rather than widening the
existing node-persistent /run/spire/sockets hostPath, to avoid changing that
hostPath's blast radius (still shared with cilium-agent's own daemonset,
unmodified).

Add a minimal-privilege leading initContainer (runAsUser/runAsGroup 0,
capabilities dropped except CHOWN/DAC_OVERRIDE) that chowns both directories
to the agent's uid/gid before the non-root agent container starts. No other
template changes needed. cilium-agent (root, privileged) keeps full access
to /run/spire/sockets regardless of its ownership.

--- a/templates/spire/agent/daemonset.yaml
+++ b/templates/spire/agent/daemonset.yaml
@@ -53,10 +53,35 @@
       initContainers:
+        - name: init-agent-socket-dir
+          image: {{ include "cilium.image" .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.initImage | quote }}
+          imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.initImage.pullPolicy }}
+          securityContext:
+            runAsNonRoot: false
+            runAsUser: 0
+            runAsGroup: 0
+            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
+            capabilities:
+              drop:
+                - ALL
+              add:
+                - CHOWN
+                - DAC_OVERRIDE
+          command:
+            - /bin/sh
+            - -c
+            - |
+              chown {{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.agent.podSecurityContext.runAsUser }}:{{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.agent.podSecurityContext.runAsGroup }} /run/spire
+              chown -R {{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.agent.podSecurityContext.runAsUser }}:{{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.agent.podSecurityContext.runAsGroup }} {{ dir .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.adminSocketPath }}
+          volumeMounts:
+            - name: spire-agent-data
+              mountPath: /run/spire
+            - name: spire-agent-socket
+              mountPath: {{ dir .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.adminSocketPath }}
         - name: init
           image: {{ include "cilium.image" .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.initImage | quote }}
           imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.authentication.mutual.spire.install.initImage.pullPolicy }}
           command:
             - /bin/sh
             - -c
             - |
               {{- tpl (.Files.Get "files/spire/wait-for-spire.bash") . | nindent 14 }}
       containers:
@@ -75,11 +75,13 @@
           volumeMounts:
+            - name: spire-agent-data
+              mountPath: /run/spire
             - name: spire-config
               mountPath: /run/spire/config
               readOnly: true
             - name: spire-bundle
               mountPath: /run/spire/bundle
             - name: spire-agent-socket
               mountPath: /run/spire/sockets
               readOnly: false
             - name: spire-agent
               mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens
@@ -126,16 +126,18 @@
       volumes:
+        - name: spire-agent-data
+          emptyDir: {}
         - name: spire-config
           configMap:
             name: spire-agent
         - name: spire-bundle
           configMap:
             name: spire-bundle
         - name: spire-agent-socket
           hostPath:
             path: /run/spire/sockets
             type: DirectoryOrCreate
         - name: spire-agent
           projected:
             sources:
             - serviceAccountToken:
                 path: spire-agent
